exit: Some(0)
--- stdout ---
Propose an action for cross-VM quorum approval.

Measures this host's own R31 extended TCB (`axtcb1-ext:`) as the proposer identity — or a clearly-labeled CI mock identity when `AXON_CI_NO_KVM=1` or the real kernel/axon-os binaries are unavailable — and writes a `VoteRequest` JSON file for peer VMs to vote on.

Usage: axon-vm quorum propose [OPTIONS] --run-id <RUN_ID> --prog <PROG> --action <ACTION> --out <OUT>

Options:
      --run-id <RUN_ID>
          Unique id for this quorum instance (binds request and responses together)

      --prog <PROG>
          Path to the Axon program (or job description) being proposed

      --action <ACTION>
          Human-readable description of the proposed action

      --out <OUT>
          Output path for the VoteRequest JSON

      --kernel <KERNEL>
          Guest kernel image to measure (default: dist/guest/vmlinuz)

      --axon-os <AXON_OS>
          axon-os binary to measure (default: sibling of this executable)

      --axon-audit <AXON_AUDIT>
          axon-audit-writer binary to measure (default: sibling; absent → R28-pending sentinel)

      --broadcast <BROADCAST>
          R33.S2e: also broadcast the VoteRequest to these peers (comma-separated "host:port" TCP-loopback addresses — the R33 spec §5.2.2 CI stand-in for real AF_VSOCK) and run the same strict-majority check `quorum check` does against whatever VoteResponses come back within --deadline-ms, exiting with the same 0/13/14 convention. Omit for the original write-only behavior (unaffected)

      --n <N>
          Required fleet size for the --broadcast quorum check (operator-configured, NOT necessarily the number of --broadcast peers). Defaults to the peer count if omitted

      --deadline-ms <DEADLINE_MS>
          Deadline for the --broadcast round trip, in milliseconds
          
          [default: 5000]

      --json
          Emit JSON output (only meaningful with --broadcast)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

